#: ../../../tutorials/basics/frames.rst:22
msgid "Frames, ticks, titles, and labels"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/basics/frames.rst:24
msgid ""
"Setting frame, ticks, titles, and labels is handled by the ``frame`` "
"parameter that many plotting methods of the :class:`pygmt.Figure` class "
"accept. This tutorial focuses on setting the ``frame`` parameter using the :"
"class:`pygmt.params.Axis` and :class:`pygmt.params.Frame` classes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/basics/frames.rst:31
msgid ""
"import pygmt\n"
"from pygmt.params import Axis, Frame"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/basics/frames.rst:40
msgid "Plot frame"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/basics/frames.rst:42
msgid ""
"By default, PyGMT does not add a frame to your plot. For example, we can "
"plot the coastlines of the world with a Mercator projection:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/basics/frames.rst:47
msgid ""
"fig = pygmt.Figure()\n"
"fig.coast(shorelines=\"1/0.5p\", region=[-180, 180, -60, 60], "
"projection=\"M15c\")\n"
"fig.show()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/basics/frames.rst:57
msgid ""
"To add the default GMT frame style to the plot, use ``frame=True`` in :meth:"
"`pygmt.Figure.basemap` or another plotting method that accepts a ``frame`` "
"parameter:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/basics/frames.rst:63
msgid ""
"fig = pygmt.Figure()\n"
"fig.coast(shorelines=\"1/0.5p\", region=[-180, 180, -60, 60], "
"projection=\"M15c\")\n"
"fig.basemap(frame=True)\n"
"fig.show()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/basics/frames.rst:76
msgid "Annotations, tick marks and grid lines"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/basics/frames.rst:78
msgid ""
"The default frame style includes tick labels (called annotations in GMT) and "
"tick marks at intervals determined by GMT, but doesn't include grid lines. "
"To control the presence and intervals of annotations, tick marks, and grid "
"lines, you can use the :class:`pygmt.params.Axis` class. The ``annot``, "
"``tick``, and ``grid`` attributes of :class:`pygmt.params.Axis` control the "
"presence and intervals of annotations, tick marks, and grid lines, "
"respectively. Setting them to ``True`` adds them at intervals determined by "
"GMT:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/basics/frames.rst:88
msgid ""
"fig = pygmt.Figure()\n"
"fig.coast(shorelines=\"1/0.5p\", region=[-180, 180, -60, 60], "
"projection=\"M15c\")\n"
"fig.basemap(frame=Axis(annot=True, tick=True, grid=True))\n"
"fig.show()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/basics/frames.rst:99
msgid ""
"To set specific intervals, pass values to ``annot``, ``tick``, and ``grid``. "
"In the example below, the annotation, tick, and gridline intervals are set "
"to 30, 7.5, and 15 degrees, respectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/basics/frames.rst:105
msgid ""
"fig = pygmt.Figure()\n"
"fig.coast(shorelines=\"1/0.5p\", region=[-180, 180, -60, 60], "
"projection=\"M15c\")\n"
"fig.basemap(frame=Axis(annot=30, tick=7.5, grid=15))\n"
"fig.show()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/basics/frames.rst:117
msgid "Title"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/basics/frames.rst:119
msgid ""
"The :class:`pygmt.params.Frame` class lets us configure frame-wide settings "
"such as titles. Combine it with an :class:`Axis` object to keep automatic "
"annotations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/basics/frames.rst:124
msgid ""
"fig = pygmt.Figure()\n"
"# region=\"TT\" specifies Trinidad and Tobago using the ISO country code\n"
"fig.coast(shorelines=\"1/0.5p\", region=\"TT\", projection=\"M15c\")\n"
"fig.basemap(frame=Frame(title=\"Trinidad and Tobago\", "
"axis=Axis(annot=True)))\n"
"fig.show()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/basics/frames.rst:138
msgid "Axis labels"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/basics/frames.rst:140
msgid ""
"Axis labels, in GMT simply called labels, can be set through the ``xaxis`` "
"and ``yaxis`` parameters of :class:`Frame`. The map boundaries (or plot "
"axes) are named as West/west/left (**W**, **w**, **l**), South/south/bottom "
"(**S**, **s**, **b**), North/north/top (**N**, **n**, **t**), and East/east/"
"right (**E**, **e**, **r**) sides of a figure. Uppercase letters (**W**, "
"**S**, **N**, **E**) draw axes with annotations and tick marks, lowercase "
"letters (**w**, **s**, **n**, **e**) draw axes with tick marks only, and "
"**l**, **b**, **t**, **r** draw plain axis lines without ticks or "
"annotations. A frame like ``Frame(axes=\"WS\")`` draws annotated west and "
"south axes only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/basics/frames.rst:150
msgid ""
"The example below uses a Cartesian projection, as GMT does not allow labels "
"to be set for geographic maps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/basics/frames.rst:155
msgid ""
"fig = pygmt.Figure()\n"
"fig.basemap(\n"
"    region=[0, 10, 0, 20],\n"
"    projection=\"X10c/8c\",\n"
"    # Plot axis with tick marks, annotations, and labels on the West and "
"South axes.\n"
"    # Plot axis with tick marks on the north and east axes\n"
"    frame=Frame(\n"
"        axes=\"WSne\",\n"
"        xaxis=Axis(annot=True, tick=True, label=\"x-axis\"),\n"
"        yaxis=Axis(annot=True, tick=True, label=\"y-axis\"),\n"
"    ),\n"
")\n"
"fig.show()"
msgstr ""

